Just for the record:

NetHack crashes when I #loot a chest and I'm near carrying capacity.

Fixed in PL8. 

Workaround: For now, just take one item at a time out of the chest. I.e.
	    go back and #loot each time.


NetHack crashes sometimes when I kick a wall/throne/drawbridge (anything that's
not an object or monster)

Fixed in PL8.

Workaround: The problem occurs when the last object you kicked disappears (food 
	    rots, gets eaten etc.). So after kicking an object that could 
	    disappear, kick another that won't (for example, keep a worthless
  	    black knife to kick around, and keep putting it back into your
	    inventory).

With a very recent breakthrough, PL8 is starting to look even closer than it
did a couple of days ago.


I ftp and download NetHack, and I get unpacking errors or invalid file sizes.

First thing to check is that you used binary mode *for each transfer*. It does
no good to ftp in binary mode, then kermit (or whatever) in ASCII. Or vice
versa.

If you are still having problems, check with the archive site. 

Linc.cis.upenn.edu has known good archives, as I think does uunet.
